  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthening the State Government</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">India is a source, destination, and transit country for men, women, and children subjected to forced labor and sex trafficking. Forced labor constitutes Indias largest trafficking problem: men, women, and children in debt bondagesometimes inherited from previous generationsare forced to work in brick kilns, rice mills, embroidery factories, and agriculture. Experts estimate millions of adults and children are victims of forced labor, and in Karnataka state, surveys show more than 30% of workers in manual labor industries are victims of forced labor. This project will equip front-line responders to respond effectively to bonded labor, ensuring that the government is proactively identifying cases and responding in a coordinated and timely manner. The project will engage with a host of local actors including district officials, anti-trafficking units, police officers, labor commissioners, public prosecutors, and judicial magistrates at the state magistrates level to encourage the state governments full buy-in and prioritization of human trafficking. Over the course of the project, hundreds of victims will be assisted and their cases will be filed, increasing local resiliency and lessening a source of illicit profit. This project will build upon local efforts and will work to reduce human trafficking and improve information sharing to target criminals and corrupt leaders and disrupt human trafficking. In addition, if successful, the project will see an increase in investigations and prosecutions, thereby serving as a deterrent to potential traffickers.</narrative>
  </description>
